-- title:
--   Wild–tame–unramified chain descends to intermediate normal pairs
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group and $q$ a prime. Let $U$ and $W$ be normal subgroups of $G$ with $U$ of finite index and $U \le W$, and assume that every $w \in W$ satisfies $w^{q^{a}} \in U$ for some $a \in \mathbb{N}$ (so $W$ is $q$-power torsion modulo $U$). Let $t,\varphi \in G$ satisfy $(t^{q})^{-1}\,\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in W$, i.e. $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in t^{q}W$, and assume that every $g \in G$ lies in $\varphi^{n}\,(\langle t\rangle \vee W)$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, where $\langle t\rangle \vee W$ is the subgroup generated by $t$ together with $W$. Let further $S$ and $H$ be subgroups of $G$ with $U \le H \le S$ and $H$ normal in $S$ (normality of $H$ viewed as a subgroup of $S$). The assertion is the existence of subgroups $P$ and $I$ of $G$ with $H \le P \le I \le S$, both $P$ and $I$ normal in $S$, such that the index of $H$ in $P$ is $q^{n}$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the index of $P$ in $I$ is not divisible by $q$, and there is an element $g \in S$ with $(g^{n})^{-1}s \in I$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$ for every $s \in S$, so that $S$ is the union of the cosets $g^{n}I$ and $S/I$ is cyclic, generated by the image of $g$.
--
--   This is the purely group-theoretic shadow of the ramification filtration of the Galois group of a local field: the axioms on $U$, $W$, $t$ and $\varphi$ encode a wild part $W$, a tame generator $t$ with $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} = t^{q}$ modulo $W$ and a Frobenius lift $\varphi$ generating the quotient, and the conclusion produces, inside any intermediate normal pair $H \trianglelefteq S$, an analogous wild–tame–unramified chain $H \le P \le I \le S$. It is used in the proof of [`ExtCitation.tame_or_descent_of_isSimple`](thm.html#ExtCitation.tame_or_descent_of_isSimple).
